  "body": "# BLOCKED / needs_followup \u2014 repaired after Mennonite REVISE\n\nThis draft records Bloodborne evidence-gap remediation only. It is **not a canonical-readiness claim, not a merge request, and must remain OPEN + DRAFT + unmerged** while the residual gaps below remain. A wholly fresh Mennonite context must audit the repaired exact head.\n\n- `Bathcat-Authored: true`\n- `Audit-Owner: Mennonite`\n- Prior audited head: `030194383bffda641fa9a0e578efd496e92767bb`\n- Repaired exact head: `e8b5e309959302876bcbe8cce36cf717d2c6e87f`\n- Repair commit: `e8b5e309959302876bcbe8cce36cf717d2c6e87f`\n\n## Edition and scope\n\nTarget: **English 2016 Bloodborne: The Card Game standalone base game only**. The Hunter's Nightmare expansion, Runes, Death Tokens, promotional material, variants, and translated material are excluded.\n\n## Official rule authority and current CMON surface\n\nOfficial 2016 CMON S3 rulebook:\n\n- URL: https://cmon-files.s3.amazonaws.com/pdf/assets_item/resource/43/Bloodborne_Rulebook__2_.pdf\n- HTTP `200`; `application/pdf`; `92,484,273` bytes; `16` pages\n- SHA-256 `e5010bc06faf0a4fc05b70228836401825a123c4dad0459233edcd318b664b38`\n- S3 Last-Modified `Sat, 30 Jul 2016 00:05:00 GMT`; ETag `dd4ffdaca078e915ebcd10f0898ac11e`\n- PDF created `2016-07-19`, modified `2016-07-30`, creator Adobe InDesign CC 2015\n\nThe 1jour-1jeu PDF is retained only as a subordinate mirror/inspection derivative, not primary rule authority.\n\nDated dynamic CMON page receipt:\n\n- `https://r.jina.ai/https://www.cmon.com/product/bloodborne-the-card-game/bloodborne-the-card-game`\n- HTTP `200`; `4,979` bytes; SHA-256 `fc29588d8a3474e2d817ef081bc84ba9d14b57b17cdbd38c288f644d1ba6e43c`\n- Current text says `Rules & More` \u2192 `Rulebook` \u2192 `79.01 MB`\n- This changing product-page surface is not an exhaustive publisher-wide support inventory and does not prove universal FAQ/errata absence.\n\n## Corrected governing ledger\n\nThe governing denominator remains **OPEN / UNKNOWN**. No governing-completeness percentage or composite score is asserted.\n\n- **CLOSED:** official English 2016 rulebook, acquired from CMON S3.\n- **CLOSED for printed general surfaces:** five Hunter Boards/player aids. They are rule-bearing through the round sequence, Trophy/scoring tracks, and collected/banked Blood Echo zones/bonuses; official rulebook pp. 4, 9, 12, and 14\u201315 sufficiently govern those surfaces.\n- **CLOSED for resolving faces:** three Monster dice. They are rule-bearing damage/combo resolvers; official rulebook p. 10 sufficiently governs their resolution.\n- **CLOSED as state/value markers:** health dials, Blood Echo tokens, Trophy tokens, and First Player token.\n- **OPEN / UNKNOWN:** complete local identity/text corpus for Starter Actions, Upgrades, Monsters, Chalice Dungeon Bosses, and Final Bosses.\n- **OPEN / UNKNOWN:** closed publisher-wide FAQ/errata/clarification/support inventory, or authoritative evidence that none exists.\n\nBounded inventory metrics remain separate from governing completeness:\n\n- Physical component-category transcription: `7 / 7`.\n- Physical card-class allocation: `25 + 32 + 5 + 18 + 7 = 87`; `87 / 87`.\n- Distinct card identity/text coverage: `UNKNOWN`.\n\n## Claim/source and review receipt repairs\n\n- All rule claims across the seven rules records, index, scout report, and source ledger now cite the official CMON S3 rulebook as `src-002`.\n- The product/support claim now records the current `Rulebook 79.01 MB` dynamic observation.\n- Ars, RPGFan, and Meeple Mountain receipts are retained as dated observations rather than immutable live-content expectations; no new review claims were added.\n\n## Reproducible visual disposition\n\nThe prior origin/raw hashes and sizes are preserved only as dated historical receipts; those bytes were not retained. The four current endpoints return Cloudflare-polished PNGs, and these exact served bytes produced the rebuilt local derivatives:\n\n| Asset | Current bytes | Current SHA-256 | `cf-polished` / prior origin size | Local derivative SHA-256 |\n|---|---:|---|---|---|\n| gameplay layout | 537,772 | `97fbd7594c380111da8546b06e9f4e085e5f42422dff3ed60a46e325cc7d1237` | `ok`, `orig_size=659031` | `60f28a1f2b0a667f9ceca25fcbc874e8263ac1e1194ace37aee411c004f1e457` |\n| monster cards | 375,927 | `5fcf12b71ed0f6988e9a18580366a381846da4c25467d594eabb53fc6984ad61` | `ok`, `orig_size=422512` | `b8cf64a7af963605f8eb8f4202fa96eee1ff1338eb656eb7cf06bf63cad698db` |\n| Action cards | 417,867 | `27345a7f7de250927fe1c45b4775f323feaf10ca5715035b317cbc59498819b4` | `ok`, `orig_size=2684174` | `72c979684084fa81394b5fa9753c5f21e3fe191153451812744143b7ed4344d0` |\n| trophies / Hunter Board | 443,750 | `88dd038787560a8932eac4ce081cd38a8aafdd8a36e45935145b0680c0d619c2` | `ok`, `orig_size=2726821` | `6c4c057adc1dd55649762fc59df621c52be168e9e7ad6fcb3d526e45293a71b0` |\n\nDeterministic transform: FFmpeg 7.1.5, Lanczos scale to `min(700,iw)` with even proportional height, libwebp quality 70/compression 6/lossy, metadata removed. Contact sheet pads derivatives to 580\u00d7260 on `#181818`, xstacks a 2\u00d72 1160\u00d7520 grid, and uses libwebp quality 72/compression 6/lossy with metadata removed. Contact sheet: 92,460 bytes, SHA-256 `b6340200d9386c65960c7c86ef14ca574d196740c1143ac67dcb3085095fb846`. It was visually inspected as four distinct, uncorrupted base-game panels with no Rune, Death Token, or Hunter's Nightmare leakage.\n\n## Scope and gates\n\nFull PR diff from base: **20 files, 886 insertions, 185 deletions**. Repair commit: **19 files, 113 insertions, 106 deletions**.\n\nFinal ordered local gates before the repair commit:\n\n- Generated BoardGames index.\n- Full OKF validation: `2,620` files clean; index fresh.\n- Intake/provenance Node tests: `31` pass, `1` skip, `0` fail.\n- Diff-aware intake validation: clean.\n- `git diff --check`: clean.\n\nExact-head CI: **SUCCESS** on run https://github.com/no-trbl-2-u/game-knowledge-base/actions/runs/30617369162, job https://github.com/no-trbl-2-u/game-knowledge-base/actions/runs/30617369162/job/91113570158, with `head_sha=e8b5e309959302876bcbe8cce36cf717d2c6e87f`. Substantive intake, provenance/visual, OKF, and write-guard steps executed successfully.\n\n## Residual HOLD request\n\n1. Complete immutable base-game card-local corpus for Starter Actions, Upgrades, Monsters, Chalice Dungeon Bosses, and Final Bosses.\n2. Closed official FAQ/errata/clarification/support inventory, or authoritative evidence that none exists.\n3. T approval of a **named immutable secondary card corpus only if the official card corpus remains unavailable**.\n\nUntil those authorities are supplied and a wholly fresh Mennonite exact-head audit returns GO, this PR remains **BLOCKED / needs_followup, OPEN + DRAFT**. Do not approve it, mark it ready, or merge it. Bathcat requests no merge.\n",
